                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">New Management, Same Old Story ...</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      
     <td bgcolor="414f6e" class="text"><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a> 
      <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
       <tr>
        <td class="text">As a warm up for the weekend's festivities, the Vis Maior Express made brief stops in Drunder, Doomfire and Reef of Coirnav last night.  Guest stars for last night's whistle stop tour included:<br><ul><li>Tallon Zek</li><li>Vallon Zek</li><li>Babnoxis, the Spider Queen</li><li>Magmaton</li><li>Hydrotha</li></ul><br>Another perfect 5 for 5 night, including a flawless Magmaton kill - all in all, not a bad start for Elyda's first night as Guild Leader.<br><br>The Loot:<br><a target="_blank" href="http://lucy.fnord.net/item.html?id=27989">Warmaster's Recurved Longbow</a> - Grats Millikin<br><a target="_blank" href="http://lucy.fnord.net/item.html?id=9462">Mask fo the Insightful</a> - Grats Viciado & Wilas<br>Elemental Silk Bracelet Pattern - Grats Leelale<br><a target="_blank" href="http://lucy.fnord.net/item.html?id=7767">Necklace of Reflected Flame</a> - Grats Genalen<br>Elemental Silk Sleeve Pattern - Grats Starlee & Wakit<br><br>Topics o' the Day - The Hulk, Harry Potter & Sex and the City.<br><ul><li>The Hulk: OK, based on the inside scoop - don't expect another Spider-Man.  Apparently the movie isn't what you might expect.  Fans looking for the action-packed feature a la Spider-Man might well be disappointed.</li><li>Harry Potter - the fifth book is out this weekend.  I have to admit, several weeks ago I gave serious thought to camping out at the local Barnes & Noble to pick up a copy at midnight (which Tovarich would have probably finished by 4 a.m. at the rate he reads!)  Then common sense took over as I headed over to Amazon.com to pre-order a copy.  Book Report coming soon...</li><li>Sex and the City -  The sixth (and apparently final) season kicks off on Sunday.Say it ain't so!!!  More fun, follies and frolics with the four femmes fatales from the streets of NYC.</li></ul>So the Outlook for this weekend?  Mad fun!<br><br><B>BREAKING NEWS</B><br>Remember the Hot Topic from two days ago?  Orrin Hatch's brilliant proposal to destroy end-user PC's for using illegal software?  Well, looks like Orrin may have to terminate his web servers first.  According to <a target="_blank" href="http://www.wired.com/news/politics/0,1283,59305,00.html">this story</a> on Wired.com's website, Herr Hatch is guilty of a little software piracy on his official US Senator website.  Game, set and match the good guys.  Remember John 8:7 Orrin?  <blockquote>He that is without sin among you, let him first cast a stone.</blockquote>  Or perhaps Luke 6:42 <blockquote>Either how canst thou say to thy brother, Brother, let me pull out the mote that is in thine eye, when thou thyself beholdest not the beam that is in thine own eye? Thou hypocrite, cast out first the beam out of thine own eye, and then shalt thou see clearly to pull out the mote that is in thy brother's eye.</blockquote><br>Translation:  <b>OOPS!!!!</b>  You blew it Orrin.  Thanks for playing, drive through.</td>
       </tr>
       <tr> 
        <td align="right" class="smItalic" height="20">Posted by <a href="mailto:" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;"> 
