                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">Plane of Fire Part II</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      
     <td bgcolor="414f6e" class="text"><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a> 
      <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
       <tr>
        <td class="text">Paid a visit to our old friend Fennin Ro the Incredibly Ugly.  We came, we cleared, we had a <B>flawless</B> kill.  Not even the token ranger death.  Better luck next time ugly.<br><br>The Loots:<br><a target="_blank" href="http://lucy.fnord.net/item.html?id=14943">Immaculate Vest of the Fire Tyrant</a> - Grats Wrenne<br><a target="_blank" href="http://lucy.fnord.net/item.html?id=12510">Gleaming Mesh Girdle</a> - Grats Dottoressa<br><br>Today's hot topic of discussion - <a target="_blank" href="http://www.cnn.com/2003/TECH/internet/06/18/downloading.music.ap/index.html">Orrin Hatch's idiotic proposal</a> to destroy the computers of people who illegally download music from the Internet.  So according to Orrin, the RIAA should have more powers to invade internet users privacy than the CIA, NSA & FBI combined.  Hey Orrin, how do you plan to compensate people whose machines get destroyed by mistake, or through malicious acts based on a technology <b>YOU</b> advocated?<br><br>The passages below are lifted from the Forums over at DSLReports.  Hey Orrin - these are voters talking to you...<br><br>How about the death penalty for Senate ethics violations or for taking soft money? How about we cut off a finger for using Federal money for personal use Senator? How about we put in imprison Senators who take contributions from the RIAA in exchange for favors? <br><br>He bitches about copyright violations. I guess every other problem in this country has been solved. There are no budget problems. No national security problems. No homeless. No one is out of work. Every student is getting 1600 on the SAT.<br><br>Perhaps Senator we should look at your role in the Salt Lake City Olympic bid. Coincidence that the FBI was denied access to you by the DoJ while you were chairman of the Senate Judiciary Committee Senator? The FBI was denied an opportunity to interview you regarding your involvement in the scandal on multiple occasions. The FBI had assembled a long paper trail of e-mails, Olympic committee documents and personal letters from you before approaching Justice officials in Washington, D.C.<br><br>/rant off</td>
       </tr>
       <tr> 
        <td align="right" class="smItalic" height="20">Posted by <a href="mailto:" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;"> 
         Shaekee
